msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-8-solver-options.ipynb:60
msgid ""
"Here we will change the absolute and relative tolerances of the "
"``IDAKLUSolver``, which is the default solver in PyBaMM. For a list of all "
"the solver options please consult the `documentation <https://docs.pybamm."
"org/en/latest/source/api/solvers/index.html>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-8-solver-options.ipynb:62
msgid ""
"We will solve the DFN with all the default options using the \"baseline\" "
"solver and a \"high-accuracy\" solver. For demonstration purposes we change "
"the cut-off voltage to 3.6 V so we can observe the different behaviour of "
"the two solver modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-8-solver-options.ipynb:-1
msgid "[7]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-8-solver-options.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"model = pybamm.lithium_ion.DFN()\n"
"param = model.default_parameter_values\n"
"param[\"Lower voltage cut-off [V]\"] = 3.6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-8-solver-options.ipynb:85
msgid ""
"Next we define two instances of the solver, one using the \"baseline\" mode "
"and the other using the \"high-accuracy\" mode. Note how we also pass the "
"tolerances as keyword arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-8-solver-options.ipynb:-1
msgid "[8]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-8-solver-options.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"solver_baseline = pybamm.IDAKLUSolver(rtol=1e-4, atol=1e-6)\n"
"solver_high_accuracy = pybamm.IDAKLUSolver(rtol=1e-8, atol=1e-12)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-8-solver-options.ipynb:107
msgid ""
"Then we can create two different simulations (one for each model, where this "
"is set using the ``solver`` keyword argument) and we solve them. We then "
"plot the results and print the solve time for each simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-8-solver-options.ipynb:-1
msgid "[9]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-8-solver-options.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"# create simulations\n"
"sim_baseline = pybamm.Simulation(model, parameter_values=param, "
"solver=solver_baseline)\n"
"sim_high_accuracy = pybamm.Simulation(\n"
"    model, parameter_values=param, solver=solver_high_accuracy\n"
")\n"
"\n"
"# solve\n"
"sim_baseline.solve([0, 3600])\n"
"print(f\"Baseline mode solve time: {sim_baseline.solution.solve_time}\")\n"
"sim_high_accuracy.solve([0, 3600])\n"
"print(f\"High accuracy mode solve time: {sim_high_accuracy.solution."
"solve_time}\")\n"
"\n"
"# plot solutions\n"
"pybamm.dynamic_plot(\n"
"    [sim_baseline, sim_high_accuracy],\n"
"    labels=[\"Baseline\", \"High accuracy\"],\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-8-solver-options.ipynb:145
msgid ""
"<pre>\n"
"Baseline mode solve time: 18.530 ms\n"
"High accuracy mode solve time: 72.792 ms\n"
"</pre>"
msgstr ""

